From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:59:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D503 code mode: typeof a tool namespace is "object"

Upstream: `typeof` answered "function" for every tool path below the root, so `typeof tools.opencode` was "function" although calling the namespace fails ("Tool 'opencode' is not callable."); only the root was "object".
Fixed: `typeof` of a namespace without a tool of its own is "object", like the root; a tool (including a callable namespace) stays "function", and so does a path that names nothing, which still fails when called. Both engines.
Scenarios: codemode-tools.test.ts "codemode tool references and failures" (types)
Upstream tests: test/tool-paths.test.ts adds "typeof is function for a tool and object for a namespace without one"

